# Week 3 – Implementation of Data Security Controls

## Telecom Sector Data Security Analyst Internship

### 1. Introduction

This week focuses on the practical implementation of data security controls in a telecom network environment. The objective is to convert the risks identified during the previous risk and vulnerability assessment into practical security measures.

A telecom environment handles sensitive information such as customer identity data, subscriber details, call records, network information, authentication data and service-related information. Therefore, security controls must protect confidentiality, integrity and availability while allowing authorized users and systems to operate efficiently.

The implementation plan in this week covers access control, multi-factor authentication, encryption, firewalls, IDS/IPS, network segmentation, secure APIs, logging and monitoring, backup protection, patch management and security testing.

